#Hard Locker PSP

A simple Payment Service Provider (PSP) system that demonstrates payment request handling, BIN-based routing, and mock communication with payment acquirers.

## Features

• REST API for payment processing
• Validation of card details (Luhn algorithm, format checks)
• Transaction lifecycle management (Pending → Approved/Denied)
• BIN routing:
  - Even digit sum → Acquirer A
  - Odd digit sum → Acquirer B
• Mock acquirer logic:
  - Approves if last digit of card number is even
  - Denies if last digit of card number is odd
• In-memory storage for transactions
• Clean architecture with layered structure and design patterns

## Tech Stack

• Java 23
• Spring Boot 3.5
• Spring Validation
• Lombok
• SLF4J + Logback for logging
• JUnit 6 for testing
• Swagger UI

To make the code easier to read, I followed generally accepted standards and principles of SOLID, and the code is also covered with tests.

## Requirements for build and launch
• Java 23
• Maven 3.9.9+

## Build and launch via bash
mvn clean install
mvn spring-boot:run

For further launch you can use command like a "java -jar halot-psp-0.0.13.jar"

## Docker

Also you can build and run app via Docker. Commands for building and running:
mvn clean package
docker build -t halot-psp .
docker run -p 8080:8080 halot-psp

## API Documentation (Swagger)

After running the application, you can explore the API via Swagger UI:
• Swagger UI: http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui/index.html
• OpenAPI JSON: http://localhost:8080/v3/api-docs

